# Pin line endings so a regenerated corpus is byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Without this, git's autocrlf on Windows normalised both sides of a comparison
# and hid a real mismatch: the blobs are LF, csv.writer emitted CRLF, and on
# Linux the two genuinely differed. CI's "committed data still matches the
# generator" step failed on every push while passing locally, which is the
# worst shape a check can have — it was telling the truth and nobody local
# could reproduce it.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
